    "text": "Idaho\nRare Idaho Flower Is Named After Death, Causes Hallucinations\nBy Greg Jannetta,\n9 hours agoMost hikers know that contact with some plants while out in nature should be avoided. A rare, unusual looking flower named after a deceased person might appear harmless visually, but if handled or consumed, can make someone ill and even cause hallucinations. I make a habit to never eat anything...",
